      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Model: Krea 2 (text encoder: Qwen3-VL 4B, type krea2; VAE: qwen_image_vae).\n1. Pick your model files in the three loaders (the ones you normally use). Do NOT add the LoRA to the model.\n2. Put 5-10 clear photos of the character in the Reference photo nodes (add more inputs on Batch Images if needed).\n3. In LoRA Prober: choose your LoRA, type its trigger word, and adjust the prompts if you like ([trigger] is replaced).\n4. Queue. The node shows progress and previews; results also go to output/lora_prober/.\n5. Read the diagnostic, then copy only the network_kwargs block into your ai-toolkit job and retrain.\n6. Optional: pick other saves of the same LoRA in compare_lora_2-4 to compare checkpoints (each costs about one more probe).\n\nKrea 2 Turbo: 8 steps, cfg 1 (set your usual steps/cfg if you use Krea 2 Raw). First run: 1 seed."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Model: Krea 2 (text encoder: Qwen3-VL 4B, type krea2; VAE: qwen_image_vae).\n1. Pick your model files in the three loaders (the ones you normally use). Do NOT add the LoRA to the model.\n2. Put 5-10 clear photos of the character in the Reference photo nodes (add more inputs on Batch Images if needed).\n3. In LoRA Prober: choose your LoRA, type its trigger word, and adjust the prompts if you like ([trigger] is replaced).\n4. Queue. The node shows progress and previews; results also go to output/lora_prober/.\n5. Read the diagnostic, then copy only the network_kwargs block into your ai-toolkit job and retrain.\n6. Optional: pick other saves of the same LoRA in compare_lora_2-4 to compare checkpoints (each costs about one more probe).\n\nKrea 2 Turbo: 8 steps, cfg 1 (set your usual steps/cfg if you use Krea 2 Raw). First run: 1 seed."
      },
